  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is a strong oxidising agent in acidic,alkaline or neutral medium as well</p><p>Thiosulphate is oxidised almost quantitatively to sulphate:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>-</mo></mmultiscripts><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p>The equivalent weight of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in the above reaction =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>158</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math></p></blockquote>"
